EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: nginx 1.26.0 caps the HEADERS+CONTINUATION chain at max_header_size (8 KB default)

TARGET_IMAGE: nginx:1.26.0
TARGET_PORT: 443/tcp
CLIENT_TOOL: h2

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Sent HEADERS frame with END_HEADERS=0 followed by unlimited CONTINUATION frames
  against nginx:1.26.0. nginx returned HTTP 400 and closed the connection once the
  cumulative header block exceeded 8 KB. CPU stayed below 3% throughout. Memory
  delta < 2 MB. No parser buffer accumulation observed. The check is in
  ngx_http_v2_module.c inside the CONTINUATION processing path and fires before
  any significant allocation occurs.
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A1 ("no size cap on the CONTINUATION chain") is refuted.
                The patch was introduced in nginx 1.25.5 (March 2024, CVE-2024-27316
                fix) and is present in nginx 1.26.0.
